[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 1"""
 date="2026-10-09T15:23:02Z"
 content="""
The obvious fixes for this are to not autoenable anything,
or to somehow prompt the user to verify autoenabled special
remotes before use.

I know that autoenabled special remotes are broadly used in the datalad
community, and losing them would probably break a great many repository
workflows.

Prompting the user is difficult because autoenabling can happen on the
first git-annex use, which could be expected to legitimately get files from
the autoenabled special remote.

I'm struggling to think of other ways to fix this though.
"""]]
